📦 GCP Data Pipeline Design (500 GB/day)

🔹 Landing Zone – Google Cloud Storage (GCS)
→ Choice: Store raw data in GCS.
→ Why: Highly scalable, durable, cost‑effective. Handles petabyte‑scale ingestion easily.

🔹 Orchestration – Cloud Composer (Airflow)
→ Choice: Use Cloud Composer for workflow scheduling.
→ Why: DAG‑based orchestration, retries, dependency management. Reliable for large daily loads.

🔹 Processing – Dataproc (Spark) / Dataflow (Apache Beam)
→ Choice: Dataproc for batch Spark jobs, Dataflow for streaming or hybrid pipelines.
→ Why: Distributed, serverless, scalable. Can process 500 GB efficiently.
→ Transformation: Apply standardization (formats, units) + business rules (aggregations, classifications).

🔹 Warehouse – BigQuery
→ Choice: Load transformed data into BigQuery.
→ Why: Serverless, columnar, highly scalable. Optimized for OLAP queries with denormalized schema.

🔹 Analytics – Looker Studio / BI Tools
→ Choice: Connect BI tools to BigQuery.
→ Why: Enables dashboards, reports, and insights for business users without infra management.
